                <head>184. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>On June 19, Japanese Prime Minister Kishi arrived in Washington for a series of
                    talks with United States officials over a 3-day period. In several of these
                    conversations, the subject of China trade controls was discussed, with Kishi
                    reiterating the interest of his government in trading with the People’s Republic
                    of China. Documentation on these conversations is scheduled for publication in
                        <ref target="frus:frus1955-57v23p1">volume XXIII</ref>.</p>
            </div>
